$$f\left( x \right) = \left\{ {\matrix{
{{x \over {1 - x}},} & {x < 0} \cr
{{x \over {1 + x}},} & {x \ge 0} \cr

} } \right.$$

$$ \Rightarrow f'\left( x \right) = \left\{ {\matrix{
{{x \over {{{\left( {1 - x} \right)}^2}}},} & {x < 0} \cr
{{x \over {{{\left( {1 + x} \right)}^2}}}} & {x \ge 0} \cr

} } \right.$$

$$\therefore$$ $$f'\left( x \right)$$ exist at everywhere.

